config FS_F2FS
	bool "F2FS filesystem support (read-only)"
	depends on BLK
	help
	  Enable read-only support for the Flash-Friendly File System (F2FS)
	  in the generic U-Boot filesystem layer.

	  This driver is intentionally limited to bootloader-safe operations:
	  probing, listing directories, obtaining file size, reading files and
	  exporting the filesystem UUID. It does not implement write, fsck,
	  checkpoint roll-forward/NAT-journal replay, encryption, casefold lookup, or decompression
	  of compressed files.

	  For reliable boot media, create the F2FS volume cleanly, run fsck.f2fs,
	  and avoid encrypted/casefolded/compressed boot files.
